What this brain follows, and how much of each source. A change in a part followed goes to Claude Code, which updates the notes naming the source in `repos:`, or opens an issue when no note does.

A repository named in a note's `repos:` and not listed here follows `everything`; listing it here replaces that. `follow` takes `everything`, `releases`, `design-records` (commits under `docs/design/`) or `"wiki:<Page>"` (commits to `docs/wiki/<Page>.md`). For example:

```yaml
subscriptions:
  - source: owner/busy-repo
    follow: [design-records, releases]
  - source: owner/other-repo
    follow: ["wiki:Security"]
```
